  "$comment": "Set-piece role packs (docs/SET_PIECES_PLAN.md, docs/CONTENT_PIPELINE.md \"Set pieces\"): what each material role a set piece's parts name is in one look, so a piece re-themes. A placement names its pack (`pack`); one that names none takes the pack listing the map's theme under `themes` (a theme belongs to one pack at most), else the theme paints it (stone: walls, trim: trim, floor and paving: floor, roof: roof, wood and metal: solids). Roles: stone, trim, floor, paving, roof, wood, metal (a library material in content/materials.json and an optional tint), facade (a room facade: map/tileOptions.ts FACADES), door (a door style: map/schema.ts DOOR_STYLES), glass (breakable, reinforced or none). `stylePack`: the Style Pack (editor/stylePacks.ts) it goes with. Maps name a pack by its id, so an id never changes. Edit, then run `node tools/content/setpieces.mjs`.",
